# whole guarantee - and unlike every other reference here there is nothing
# else to pin: `regexp` is in the standard library, so the compiler the
# digest names carries the implementation that answers.
#
# **This is RE2's lineage and is not RE2.** Go's own documentation says
# `regexp/syntax` is RE2's syntax, which is why one dialect row can be read
# off it; the C++ RE2 is a separate implementation with constructs Go's does
# not have (`\C`) and an options struct Go exposes as two constructors. The
# dialect is named `re2` because that is what the family is called and what
# documentation/dialects.md has called it since the table was written, and
# the pin names the implementation that actually answers. A second reference
# would be the way to tell the two apart, and there is not one here.
#
